Z||000000||contra||07-23-2000||09:39 PM||||I'm just curious how the fiero V6 would stand up against the following cars just out of plain curiosity. if anybody's raced any of these cars post some stories...<P>Fiero VS:  Miata<BR>           Stealth<BR>           93 and up 300ZX<BR>           VW GTI<BR>           Older Eagle Talons<BR>           Acura Legend<BR>           Honda De Sol<P>i'm sure there is more but i can't think of any right now, i'm just wondering because those are the cars i see being riced up (not counting the dodge stealth), and i'm just curious how the V6 fiero would stand up against them||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||07-23-2000||11:16 PM||||One of my friends from high school knows a guy at his college with a 95 dodge stealth, and based on what I've heard about the car... a fiero wouldn't stand a chance against it..<P>not sure about the others.. probably could beat a del sol, doesn't it just have a civic engine in it? (which would make sense, seeing as it is a civic... just like half the other cars honda makes.. hehe)<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||07-23-2000||11:39 PM||||<P>Fiero VS:  Miata<BR>           Stealth<BR>           93 and up 300ZX<BR>           VW GTI<BR>           Older Eagle Talons<BR>           Acura Legend<BR>           Honda De Sol<P>Let's see the Miata is better in the slaloms than the Fiero.  Those guys always beat us on SOLO races.  The good part is that the Miata sucks in straight line acceleration and high speed highway work.<BR>The stealth if it is a twin turbo no chance in straight line acceleration but might be able to beat it on the slalom since the Stealth is very very heavy.<BR>300ZX non tubo has no chance but the turbo one will make you cry. I don't know much about the slalom of these cars since none of them run at our SOLO events.<BR>VW GTI is not even worth to race.  They do not have straight acceleration and on the slalom course it's quite funny seeing them lift the outside rear tire looking like a little dog trying to do his bussiness.<BR>Eagle talons are a fare comparison.  They are equall to the Fiero on slalom might be a bit better on straight line acceleartion if the owner had some turbo work done.<BR>Acura legend and Honda Delsol are much like the VW not worth racing.  On the solo tracks they do not have the proper handling and in straight line acceleration well it's a Honda. Lots of high end HP and no low end troque.  <BR>From a personal experience stay away from a Proche Boxer S one creamed me on the highway.  I drove home crying could not believe how slow my car is on off ramps and acceleration at 150kph compared to one of those.  <P>Cheers||||reg||1
Z||000003||contra||07-24-2000||06:55 AM||||about the 300ZX, i have seen some videos of those cars doing slalom and they're pretty damn good at it too. Please do not flame me on this next remark, but i think my next car when i am a bit older and have more money will be a 300ZX twin turbo, or maybe a new supra (i dont know much about the supras, but i like the look of them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Taijiguy||07-24-2000||08:38 AM||||Don't feel bad about the loss to a Porsche, Sillhouette, a while back (BEFORE the latest rebuild) I got absolutely *CRUSHED* by a Lexus (300SC I believe, it was dark) I couldn't believe how quick that car accelerated from 45mph. He stomped the gas to the floor, and was past me before I could even drop a gear. I made up my mind that night I had to make some MAJOR changes to how my GT was set up. I'll be looking for a re-match here shortly......<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000005||b lo 0||07-24-2000||09:37 AM||||Just another coupla VS-  I got together with some buddies of mine, and promptly spanked a '94 Bronco-with a heavily built Mustang Cobra 5.0 in it- and a '93 Gran Prix.  Now, the '79 Mustang Cobra I didn't fare so well against.  Maybe when I get my nitrous...<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car||||reg||4
Z||000006||DJRice||07-24-2000||09:40 AM||||Miatas are a fun conquest...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I was out for a ride one evening (a long while back now) when a Red Miata (Tag "RED FUN") rolls up beside me.  He looks over and drops a gear so I could here the engine rev.  Initially I wasnt going to bother with him, but the light ahead of us turned yellow.  He revved his engine as we waited for the green light and when it turned I dropped the hammer.  I dont know if he missed his jump off the line or what but I had by at least a car length by the time my Auto went to 3rd.  <P><P>------------------<BR>Dillon - Titusville, FL<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"Matched Perfect and Staggered Special"||||reg||1
